# WHAT A CHECKOUT OF THIS REPO IS MADE OF, decided here rather than by whichever
# machine happens to clone it.
#
# There was no .gitattributes, so every tracked file's line endings came from the
# cloning machine's core.autocrlf. This seat has `input` and a clean Windows 11 VM
# has `true` - Git for Windows' own installer default - so the same commit
# materialised as LF here and as CRLF there. MEASURED 2026-08-21: cloned with
# `-c core.autocrlf=true`, all eight tests/fixtures/brief/*.md arrive with CRLF,
# and New-FmBrief's byte-for-byte comparison against them fails seven times on a
# machine where nothing is wrong. docs/windows-e2e-evidence.md section 40.3 has it.
#
# LF is not a preference here: state files, briefs and wake records are a
# byte-for-byte shared contract with a Linux firstmate, and every fixture this
# suite compares against is a copy of one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exception, because a batch file is a Windows format and CRLF is its native
# form. cmd.exe tolerates LF for the linear shape bin/fm-dictate.cmd has today,
# but not reliably once a file grows a label or a continuation, so the safe
# ending is pinned rather than relied on.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
